<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>DW - English for Africa</title><subtitle type="html">News, Analysis and Service from Germany and Europe - in 30 Languages</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-africa</id><updated>2026-09-17T19:46:47Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-africa" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-12756?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-africa" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>South Africa: Police find 9th body of woman amid spree fears</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f92321a33be324f0ed872a65c10e218707da52797ec0f9280acb13ac9eb95031</id><updated>2026-09-17T19:46:47Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T12:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-africa-police-find-9th-body-of-woman-amid-spree-fears/a-79310945--14212b985f47.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-africa-police-find-9th-body-of-woman-amid-spree-fears/a-79310945?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Police in South Africa have discovered the bodies of nine women east of Johannesburg in two months, stoking fears of a serial killer or group of killers.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Congo's Ebola epidemic may have gone undetected for months</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4a0ce36748491a6f1dda4c3344435c688ae3b1bd9aef122bde03ca344e0960c7</id><updated>2026-09-17T19:46:47Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T11:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/congo-s-ebola-epidemic-may-have-gone-undetected-for-months/a-79281803--d84e2884bf66.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/congo-s-ebola-epidemic-may-have-gone-undetected-for-months/a-79281803?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The deadliest Ebola outbreak on record in the Democratic Republic of Congo may have begun months before it was first declared in May.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>US announces South Africa visa curbs over race claims</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b2be69a837419a4a221e3d6713cd3ac042d22e805511c57fe3c891e23c166efc</id><updated>2026-09-17T19:46:47Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T10:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-announces-south-africa-visa-curbs-over-race-claims/a-79288287--ba8545978a2c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-announces-south-africa-visa-curbs-over-race-claims/a-79288287?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The visa restriction policy targets South African nationals who US Secretary of State Marco Rubio claims are responsible for "race-based discrimination" against white citizens.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Global Gender Gap Report: Women's hard-won gains 'fragile'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e6a386fb9b979983b173d0cfb972e635f20052380b8c7fb4164a23eb4292f8a5</id><updated>2026-09-17T19:46:47Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T10:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/global-gender-gap-report-women-s-hard-won-gains-fragile/a-79280086--9ed95bd98a77.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/global-gender-gap-report-women-s-hard-won-gains-fragile/a-79280086?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Two decades of progress toward gender parity is at risk as women's political representation declines, according to a new World Economic Forum report. At the current pace, the remaining gap could take 120 years to close.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Africa's richest man Dangote's IPO out of reach in Nigeria</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:12f94d32b1c23717f3b19066593b9ca1216180390fdfa2393d91fd67721e90cc</id><updated>2026-09-17T19:46:47Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T14:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/africa-s-richest-man-dangote-s-ipo-out-of-reach-in-nigeria/a-79263398--03e0d1756308.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/africa-s-richest-man-dangote-s-ipo-out-of-reach-in-nigeria/a-79263398?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Dangote seeks $1.6 billion from investors to finance a $14.3 billion expansion and thus double the oil refinery's capacity. The offer could give millions of Nigerians a stake in the company. But who can truly afford it?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Uber leaves 2 key African markets — and drivers in despair</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:45cd5c9fc75c668f4aa68c73ca794b79bf4b77060b745efe420081a2f951095f</id><updated>2026-09-17T19:46:47Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T07:56:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uber-leaves-2-key-african-markets-and-drivers-in-despair/a-79232189--6991d13e0e30.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uber-leaves-2-key-african-markets-and-drivers-in-despair/a-79232189?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Uber's departure from Nigeria and Uganda has left countless customers high and dry. But what about drivers? With fuel prices, maintenance, and other operating costs rising, many say they're struggling to make a living.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
